abstract:
Grid search wastes almost all of its budget re-testing values of parameters that do not matter. Random search fixes that; Bayesian optimisation goes further by learning from every trial where to look next. This topic covers the search-space geometry argument, how Optuna's TPE sampler models good and bad trials separately, define-by-run search spaces, pruning, parameter importance, and the cross-validation discipline that keeps a tuned score honest.}
